ding Business Analytics, Information Systems, Cybersecurity Management, and Artificial Intelligence for Business. We also offer a certificate in Artificial Intelligence for Business and Cybersecurity Management. Minimum Qualifications: Required: Doctorate in information systems or a closely related field by the date of appointment (or must be completed by December 31, 2027, for appointment to a second year), with prior experience in teaching information systems courses in a business school environment. Consideration may be given to candidates with an interest in research and teaching related to cybersecurity management; previous research success and/or a promising research pipeline in cybersecurity; relevant work and leadership experience to advance our Information Systems & Cybersecurity Management program, and its alignment with emerging digital and AI-driven business practices. Additional Position Information (if applicable) Required Application Documents Cover letter, curriculum vitae, evidence of teaching effectiveness through recent teaching evaluations, teaching philosophy, research statement, and graduate transcripts. Special Instructions (if applicable) Faculty members will be talking to interested candidates at AMCIS. Inquiries about the position can be directed to Dr. Joseph Nwankpa (nwankpjk@miamioh.edu). Screening of applications will begin in early September 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Additional Information A criminal background check is required. All campuses are smoke- and tobacco-free campuses. This organization participates in E-Verify. Reasonable Accommodations Requests for reasonable accommodations for disabilities related to employment should be directed to ADAFacultyStaff@miamioh.edu or 513-529-3560. Questions and follow-ups regarding requests should also be directed here. Miami University Values Statement Miami University is a scholarly community whose members believe that a liberal education is grounded in qualities 